   "solution": "$\\alpha = \\sum_{r=0}^{n}(4r^{2} + 2r + 1) \\cdot {}^{n}C_{r}$\n$\\alpha = 4\\sum_{r=0}^{n} r^{2} \\cdot \\frac{n}{r} \\cdot {}^{n-1}C_{r-1} + 2\\sum_{r=0}^{n} r \\cdot \\frac{n}{r} \\cdot {}^{n-1}C_{r-} + \\sum_{r=0}^{n}{}^{n}C_{r}$\n$+4n\\sum_{r=0}^{n}{}^{n-1}C_{r-1} + 2n\\sum_{r=0}^{n}{}^{n-1}C_{r-1} + \\sum_{r=0}^{n}{}^{n}C_{r}$\n$\\alpha = 4n(n - 1) \\cdot 2^{n-2} + 4n \\cdot 2^{n-1} + 2n \\cdot 2^{n-1} + 2^{n}$\n$\\alpha = 2^{n-2}[4n(n-1) + 8n + 4n + 4]$\n$\\alpha = 2^{n-2}[4n^{2} + 8n + 4]$\n$\\alpha = 2n(n + 1)^{2}$\n$\\beta = \\sum_{r=0}^{n}\\frac{{}^{n}C_{r}}{r + 1} + \\frac{1}{n + 1}$\n$= \\sum_{r=0}^{n}\\frac{{}^{n+1}C_{r+1}}{n + 1} + \\frac{1}{n + 1}$\n$= \\frac{1}{n + 1}\\left(1 + {}^{n+1}C_{1} + \\ldots. + {}^{n+1}C_{n+1}\\right)$\n$= \\frac{2^{n+1}}{n + 1}$\n$\\frac{2\\alpha}{\\beta} = \\frac{2^{n+1}(n + 1)^{2}}{2^{n+1}} \\cdot (n + 1) = (n + 1)^{3}$\n$140 < (n + 1)^{3} < 281$\n$n = 4 \\Rightarrow (n + 1)^{3} = 125$\n$n = 5 \\Rightarrow (n + 1)^{3} = 216$\n$n = 6 \\Rightarrow (n + 1)^{3} = 343$\n$\\therefore n = 5$",
